@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Available and very-busy expression analysis

rectangle "CodePropertyGraph\nimmutable AST + CFG" as CPG #F1F3F5
rectangle "BlockCfg\nreachable nodes + typed edges" as CFG #D3F9D8
rectangle "ExprFacts + VarFacts\ncanonical expressions\nGEN / KILL by operand definitions" as FACTS #FFF3BF
rectangle "Forward-Must availability\n<latex>A_{in}[n]=\bigcap_{p\in pred(n)}A_{out}[p]</latex>\n<latex>A_{out}[n]=GEN[n]\cup(A_{in}[n]\setminus KILL[n])</latex>" as AVAILABLE #DBE4FF
rectangle "Backward-Must anticipability\n<latex>B_{out}[n]=\bigcap_{s\in succ(n)}B_{in}[s]</latex>\n<latex>B_{in}[n]=GEN[n]\cup(B_{out}[n]\setminus KILL[n])</latex>" as BUSY #E5DBFF
rectangle "DominatorTree\nnearest dominating occurrence\nnearest common dominator" as DOM #C3FAE8
rectangle "AvailableExpressions\navailable_in + redundant pairs" as CSE #FFE8CC
rectangle "VeryBusyExpressions\nbusy_out + hoistable placements" as PRE #FFE3E3

CPG --> CFG : block_cfg(function)
CPG --> FACTS : structural syntax facts
CFG --> AVAILABLE : forward block order
CFG --> BUSY : reverse block order
FACTS --> AVAILABLE : MustBits transfer
FACTS --> BUSY : MustBits transfer
CPG --> DOM : cfg_projection(function)
AVAILABLE --> CSE : per-node replay
DOM --> CSE : first dominates second
BUSY --> PRE : per-node replay
DOM --> PRE : placement dominates evaluations

note bottom of CSE
  Candidate evidence is conservative.
  Separate branch computations may establish availability
  without yielding a single dominating redundant pair.
end note

note bottom of PRE
  Reports stay out of graph.
  Language-aware clients must validate side effects,
  traps, floating-point policy, and concurrency.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#F1F3F5>| immutable source graph |
  |<#D3F9D8>| control-flow substrate |
  |<#FFF3BF>| canonical expression facts |
  |<#DBE4FF>| forward-Must availability |
  |<#E5DBFF>| backward-Must anticipability |
  |<#C3FAE8>| dominance evidence |
  |<#FFE8CC>| advisory CSE evidence |
  |<#FFE3E3>| advisory PRE evidence |
endlegend
@enduml
